{"id":"NCT07253051","title":"BRCA Mutation Carriers' Platform a Multicenter Study","official":"BRCA Mutation Carriers' Platform, a Multicenter Study","summary":"Subjects who carry mutations in breast cancer susceptibility genes 1 and 2 (BRCA1 and BRCA2 genes) are at higher risk of developing cancers. Despite the cumulative amount of evidence published in the literature in the last two decades, the management of BRCA mutation carriers is still not completely defined.\n\nSince the prevalence of the mutation is estimated to be 1:400 - 1:500 individuals, the total number of BRCA mutation carriers should be around 140.000 - 150.000 in the Italian population. It is estimated that 87% of women with BRCA mutations will experience, in their lifetime, a tumor with a genetic origin. About 20% of the 5200 ovarian cancer cases diagnosed each year in Italy has a genetic origin and could potentially be the object of primary prevention. To date, and to the best of our knowledge, a national prospective data collection on women with BRCA mutations has not been yet established.","conditions":["BRCA1 Mutation","BRCA2 Mutation"],"interventions":[{"type":"OTHER","name":"Registration of clinical datas in the platform"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* All women who are 18 years of age or older;\n* All women who known to be carriers of a pathogenetic mutation class 4 and 5 of the International Agency of Research on Cancer classification) of the BRCA1 or BRCA2 genes.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* Age \\< 18 years old;\n* No pathogenetic mutation carriers.","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"FEMALE","healthy":false,"studyType":"OBSERVATIONAL","purpose":"","enrollment":10000,"start":"2025-04-05","pcd":"2045-04-01","upd":"2025-11-28","sponsor":"Fondazione Policlinico Universitario Agostino Gemelli IRCCS","areas":["other"],"central":["Anna Fagotti · +390630157004 · anna.fagotti@policlinicogemelli.it"],"sites":[{"f":"Malzoni Research Hospital","city":"Avellino","pr":"","zip":"83100","s":"